flowchart TB
  accTitle: Determine this for a function invocation
  accDescr: Read top to bottom and stop at the first matching rule. Arrows use lexical this. Construction uses a new instance. Ordinary calls to bound functions retain their bound receiver. Otherwise call or apply supply a receiver, method calls use their base object, and plain calls depend on the function's strictness.
  arrow("1. Arrow function?<br/>Yes: enclosing this")
  construct("2. Called with new?<br/>Yes: new instance")
  bound("3. Already bound?<br/>Yes: bound receiver")
  explicit("4. Using call or apply?<br/>Yes: supplied receiver")
  method("5. Method invocation?<br/>Yes: base object")
  plain("6. Plain function call<br/>Strict: undefined<br/>Sloppy: globalThis")
  arrow -->|No| construct
  construct -->|No| bound
  bound -->|No| explicit
  explicit -->|No| method
  method -->|No| plain
